Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.02,0:00:03.91,Caption,,0,0,0,,Three facts make this book almost\Nimpossible to dismiss.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:03.96,0:00:07.95,Caption,,0,0,0,,First: its parchment was made more than six\Ncenturies ago.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:08.00,0:00:12.38,Caption,,0,0,0,,Second: at least five different people\Nappear to have written it.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:12.43,0:00:16.32,Caption,,0,0,0,,Third: after generations of cryptographers,\Nlinguists, historians,
Dialogue: 1,0:00:16.37,0:00:19.59,Caption,,0,0,0,,and computer scientists, no one can read a\Nsingle page with
Dialogue: 1,0:00:19.64,0:00:23.24,Caption,,0,0,0,,scholarly agreement. Inside Yale's Beinecke\NLibrary, the object is
Dialogue: 1,0:00:23.29,0:00:27.07,Caption,,0,0,0,,cataloged simply as Manuscript 408. Its two\Nhundred thirty-four pages
Dialogue: 1,0:00:27.12,0:00:31.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,contain impossible plants, rotating skies,\Nhuman figures, and thousands
Dialogue: 1,0:00:31.05,0:00:34.21,Caption,,0,0,0,,of words in an alphabet found nowhere else.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:34.26,0:00:37.26,Caption,,0,0,0,,If it is a cipher, the key has vanished.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:37.31,0:00:40.80,Caption,,0,0,0,,If it is a language, every known speaker is\Ngone.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:40.85,0:00:44.63,Caption,,0,0,0,,And if it is a hoax, someone invested\Nextraordinary time, skill,
Dialogue: 1,0:00:44.68,0:00:47.45,Caption,,0,0,0,,and money to create a lie that has survived\Nfor six
Dialogue: 1,0:00:47.50,0:00:51.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,hundred years. This is not the story of a\Nsolved code.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:51.33,0:00:54.93,Caption,,0,0,0,,It is the evidence behind the book no one\Ncan read.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:54.98,0:00:57.80,Caption,,0,0,0,,Begin with the object, not the theories.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:57.85,0:01:01.14,Caption,,0,0,0,,The Voynich Manuscript is a small parchment\Ncodex, about nine by
Dialogue: 1,0:01:01.19,0:01:04.80,Caption,,0,0,0,,six inches. Radiocarbon analysis of four\Nsamples dated its animal-skin
Dialogue: 1,0:01:04.85,0:01:07.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,pages to between 1404 and 1438.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:07.25,0:01:11.01,Caption,,0,0,0,,Its inks and pigments use materials\Ncompatible with historical manuscript
Dialogue: 1,0:01:11.06,0:01:14.76,Caption,,0,0,0,,production. Important distinction:\Nradiocarbon dates the parchment,
Dialogue: 1,0:01:14.81,0:01:17.58,Caption,,0,0,0,,not each stroke of ink. By itself, it\Ncannot prove the
Dialogue: 1,0:01:17.63,0:01:20.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,exact day the writing was added.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:20.09,0:01:23.79,Caption,,0,0,0,,But together with the book's physical\Nconstruction, pigments, wear,
Dialogue: 1,0:01:23.84,0:01:27.45,Caption,,0,0,0,,and later ownership record, the evidence\Nstrongly supports a genuinely
Dialogue: 1,0:01:27.50,0:01:30.79,Caption,,0,0,0,,medieval codex. Then paleographer Lisa\NFagin Davis examined tiny
Dialogue: 1,0:01:30.84,0:01:35.17,Caption,,0,0,0,,differences in the handwriting: how glyphs\Nlean, connect, and repeat.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:35.22,0:01:38.25,Caption,,0,0,0,,Her conclusion was not one scribe, but\Nfive.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:38.30,0:01:41.02,Caption,,0,0,0,,That changes the scale of the mystery.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:41.07,0:01:44.67,Caption,,0,0,0,,Several people seem to have learned the\Nsame unfamiliar writing system
Dialogue: 1,0:01:44.72,0:01:47.59,Caption,,0,0,0,,and coordinated a large illustrated book.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:47.64,0:01:50.31,Caption,,0,0,0,,We still do not know what they wrote.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:50.36,0:01:52.97,Caption,,0,0,0,,But we know this was organized work.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:53.02,0:01:57.51,Caption,,0,0,0,,Open the manuscript and it divides into six\Nvisual worlds.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:57.56,0:02:00.92,Caption,,0,0,0,,The largest section resembles an herbal.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:00.97,0:02:04.84,Caption,,0,0,0,,Each page presents a plant, but many roots,\Nleaves, and flowers
Dialogue: 1,0:02:04.89,0:02:09.25,Caption,,0,0,0,,resist reliable identification. Next come\Nastronomical and astrological
Dialogue: 1,0:02:09.30,0:02:13.30,Caption,,0,0,0,,pages: suns, stars, zodiac-like rings, and\Ncircular diagrams that
Dialogue: 1,0:02:13.35,0:02:17.52,Caption,,0,0,0,,almost resemble calendars. A third section\Nshows small human figures
Dialogue: 1,0:02:17.57,0:02:21.13,Caption,,0,0,0,,linked by pools, pipes, and flowing shapes.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:21.18,0:02:25.54,Caption,,0,0,0,,Curators call it biological or\Nbalneological—connected with bathing—but
Dialogue: 1,0:02:25.59,0:02:29.58,Caption,,0,0,0,,that label describes the imagery, not its\Nmeaning.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:29.63,0:02:33.93,Caption,,0,0,0,,Cosmological foldouts expand into elaborate\Nmedallions.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:33.98,0:02:38.78,Caption,,0,0,0,,Pharmaceutical pages pair plant parts with\Nvessel-like objects.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:38.83,0:02:42.58,Caption,,0,0,0,,The final pages look like short recipes,\Neach entry marked by
Dialogue: 1,0:02:42.63,0:02:47.92,Caption,,0,0,0,,a star-shaped flower. Every image feels one\Nstep away from recognition.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:47.97,0:02:51.71,Caption,,0,0,0,,That is the trap. A plant can look\Nmedicinal without matching
Dialogue: 1,0:02:51.76,0:02:55.76,Caption,,0,0,0,,a species. A circle can look astronomical\Nwithout mapping a known
Dialogue: 1,0:02:55.81,0:02:59.73,Caption,,0,0,0,,sky. Because the labels cannot be read,\Npictures cannot securely
Dialogue: 1,0:02:59.78,0:03:04.96,Caption,,0,0,0,,explain the words—and the words cannot\Nsecurely explain the pictures.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:05.01,0:03:08.58,Caption,,0,0,0,,The ownership trail begins in imperial\NPrague.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:08.63,0:03:12.85,Caption,,0,0,0,,Yale identifies Holy Roman Emperor Rudolf\Nthe Second as the manuscript's
Dialogue: 1,0:03:12.90,0:03:16.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,first confirmed owner. A surviving account\Nsays he paid six hundred
Dialogue: 1,0:03:16.87,0:03:20.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,gold ducats and believed the work might be\Nby the English
Dialogue: 1,0:03:20.25,0:03:24.12,Caption,,0,0,0,,thinker Roger Bacon. Modern scholarship\Ntreats that attribution as
Dialogue: 1,0:03:24.17,0:03:28.15,Caption,,0,0,0,,speculation. The book later passed through\Nthe library of pharmacist
Dialogue: 1,0:03:28.20,0:03:32.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,Jacobus de Tepenec and then to Prague\Nalchemist Georgius Baresch.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:32.95,0:03:36.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,Baresch called it a riddle and asked the\Ncelebrated Jesuit scholar
Dialogue: 1,0:03:36.87,0:03:40.61,Caption,,0,0,0,,Athanasius Kircher for help. In 1666,\NJohannes Marcus Marci sent
Dialogue: 1,0:03:40.66,0:03:44.35,Caption,,0,0,0,,the manuscript to Kircher in Rome with a\Nletter still preserved
Dialogue: 1,0:03:44.40,0:03:48.15,Caption,,0,0,0,,inside it. Then, silence. For more than two\Ncenturies, the trail
Dialogue: 1,0:03:48.20,0:03:52.18,Caption,,0,0,0,,becomes uncertain. In 1912, Polish-American\Nrare-book dealer Wilfrid
Dialogue: 1,0:03:52.23,0:03:56.22,Caption,,0,0,0,,Voynich purchased it from a Jesuit college\Nnear Rome.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:56.27,0:04:00.55,Caption,,0,0,0,,The mystery took his name. After passing\Nthrough later owners, bookseller
Dialogue: 1,0:04:00.60,0:04:03.75,Caption,,0,0,0,,H. P. Kraus donated it to Yale in 1969.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:03.80,0:04:08.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,Today every page is online. Access is no\Nlonger the problem.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:08.25,0:04:10.16,Caption,,0,0,0,,Interpretation is.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:10.21,0:04:13.92,Caption,,0,0,0,,Look closely and the writing is not random\Nscribbling.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:13.97,0:04:16.31,Caption,,0,0,0,,It runs mainly left to right.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:16.36,0:04:20.01,Caption,,0,0,0,,Glyphs form repeated word-like units. Some\Nforms favor the beginning
Dialogue: 1,0:04:20.06,0:04:23.72,Caption,,0,0,0,,of a line; others cluster near certain\Nillustrations.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:23.77,0:04:27.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,Neighboring words can differ by only one\Nsign.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:27.09,0:04:31.01,Caption,,0,0,0,,Researchers have tested frequency,\Nrepetition, entropy, and relationships
Dialogue: 1,0:04:31.06,0:04:34.55,Caption,,0,0,0,,between sections. Some results resemble\Npatterns found in natural
Dialogue: 1,0:04:34.60,0:04:39.07,Caption,,0,0,0,,language. That sounds like a\Nbreakthrough—until the caution arrives.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:39.12,0:04:42.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,A cipher can preserve statistical\Nstructure.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:42.33,0:04:44.78,Caption,,0,0,0,,A lost shorthand can create it.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:44.83,0:04:48.38,Caption,,0,0,0,,A specially designed notation system can\Ncreate it.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:48.43,0:04:52.30,Caption,,0,0,0,,Even an algorithm for generating\Nmeaningless text can produce convincing
Dialogue: 1,0:04:52.35,0:04:56.49,Caption,,0,0,0,,repetition. And because some glyphs are\Nambiguous, changing the transcription
Dialogue: 1,0:04:56.54,0:05:00.25,Caption,,0,0,0,,can change the statistics. Linguists Claire\NBowern and Luke Lindemann
Dialogue: 1,0:05:00.30,0:05:03.95,Caption,,0,0,0,,reviewed this evidence and reached a\Ncareful conclusion: computation
Dialogue: 1,0:05:04.00,0:05:07.27,Caption,,0,0,0,,can eliminate weak ideas and reveal\Nstructure, but it has not
Dialogue: 1,0:05:07.32,0:05:10.81,Caption,,0,0,0,,established one accepted language or\Ndecipherment.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:10.86,0:05:13.69,Caption,,0,0,0,,Patterns prove that there is a system.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:13.74,0:05:16.85,Caption,,0,0,0,,They do not yet prove what the system says.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:16.90,0:05:20.26,Caption,,0,0,0,,Four broad explanations remain in\Ncontention.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:20.31,0:05:24.52,Caption,,0,0,0,,Theory one: an ordinary language hidden by\Nsubstitution, abbreviation,
Dialogue: 1,0:05:24.57,0:05:28.44,Caption,,0,0,0,,or a complex cipher. The regularity\Nfits—but no proposed key produces
Dialogue: 1,0:05:28.49,0:05:31.96,Caption,,0,0,0,,a coherent reading across the whole\Nmanuscript.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:32.01,0:05:35.65,Caption,,0,0,0,,Theory two: a lost shorthand or invented\Nalphabet.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:35.70,0:05:39.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,This could explain why the text looks\Nlinguistic while resisting
Dialogue: 1,0:05:39.33,0:05:43.15,Caption,,0,0,0,,familiar scripts. Without a parallel text,\Nit is extremely difficult
Dialogue: 1,0:05:43.20,0:05:46.78,Caption,,0,0,0,,to test. Theory three: a constructed\Nnotation meaningful only to
Dialogue: 1,0:05:46.83,0:05:50.98,Caption,,0,0,0,,a small community—perhaps medical,\Nreligious, or scholarly.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:51.03,0:05:54.73,Caption,,0,0,0,,Five scribal hands make a shared convention\Nplausible, but they do
Dialogue: 1,0:05:54.78,0:05:58.71,Caption,,0,0,0,,not reveal its purpose. Theory four: an\Nelaborate hoax.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:58.76,0:06:02.46,Caption,,0,0,0,,Experiments show that rule-based nonsense\Ncan imitate some Voynich
Dialogue: 1,0:06:02.51,0:06:06.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,statistics. But “meaningless” does not\Nexplain the costly parchment,
Dialogue: 1,0:06:06.65,0:06:10.80,Caption,,0,0,0,,sustained artwork, multiple writers, or the\Nintended buyer.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:10.85,0:06:14.84,Caption,,0,0,0,,A hoax would still be a remarkable\Norganized production.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:14.89,0:06:18.87,Caption,,0,0,0,,Each theory explains one clue and collides\Nwith another.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:18.92,0:06:22.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,Cipher explains secrecy, but not the\Nmissing key.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:22.55,0:06:25.97,Caption,,0,0,0,,Language explains structure, but not\Nidentity.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:26.02,0:06:28.92,Caption,,0,0,0,,Hoax explains failure—but not effort.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:28.97,0:06:32.38,Caption,,0,0,0,,Artificial intelligence has now joined the\Nhunt, comparing glyph
Dialogue: 1,0:06:32.43,0:06:36.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,sequences and candidate languages at\Nenormous scale.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:36.05,0:06:39.41,Caption,,0,0,0,,It can find similarities no person would\Nnotice.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:39.46,0:06:43.35,Caption,,0,0,0,,It can also force a dramatic answer from a\Nbad assumption.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:43.40,0:06:46.81,Caption,,0,0,0,,A real solution needs more than a viral\Nheadline.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:46.86,0:06:50.27,Caption,,0,0,0,,The method must be reproducible. The\Ngrammar and vocabulary must
Dialogue: 1,0:06:50.32,0:06:54.16,Caption,,0,0,0,,make historical sense. And the same key\Nmust produce consistent readings
Dialogue: 1,0:06:54.21,0:06:58.11,Caption,,0,0,0,,across botanical pages, circular diagrams,\Nand plain text.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:58.16,0:07:02.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,No public claim has yet crossed that\Nthreshold to scholarly consensus.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:02.75,0:07:06.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,Perhaps the missing key survives in an\Nuncataloged archive.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:06.75,0:07:10.75,Caption,,0,0,0,,Perhaps this is a writing system with no\Nsurviving relative.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:10.80,0:07:14.16,Caption,,0,0,0,,Or perhaps the manuscript was designed to\Ncreate the feeling of
Dialogue: 1,0:07:14.21,0:07:17.94,Caption,,0,0,0,,meaning without ever surrendering it. Here\Nis what the evidence allows
Dialogue: 1,0:07:17.99,0:07:21.56,Caption,,0,0,0,,us to say: the Voynich Manuscript is a\Ngenuine medieval codex,
Dialogue: 1,0:07:21.61,0:07:25.24,Caption,,0,0,0,,produced by multiple hands, filled with an\Nunidentified script whose
Dialogue: 1,0:07:25.29,0:07:29.23,Caption,,0,0,0,,meaning remains unresolved. The pages are\Nopen to everyone.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:29.28,0:07:32.91,Caption,,0,0,0,,The answer is not. This is RAHASYA: Global\NMysteries.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:32.96,0:07:36.15,Caption,,0,0,0,,Which theory best fits the evidence—and\Nwhat does it fail to
Dialogue: 1,0:07:36.20,0:07:37.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,explain?
